{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-wasm.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:35:23.251071Z","id":"7e91434f9bd90b956ab7c5a17a3dc20736797b9733de4fad82e796ac55075b46","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"No longer true: scripts/quality_gates.sh:158 runs scripts/check-wasm.sh (the thread's close, cc73bc73), and the script now also checks clax-content-git (scripts/check-wasm.sh:2-4).","supersedes":"f7a7babd97c31991fc6c0cffaff7a09bd20a7883e38d1a84d0622e6c162e102d","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-clients.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:23.153271Z","id":"d5bf7790d56e2ef77e9188e4f838271a7fa7c2df25d43e72e2f571340e7ea94a","body":{"detail":"The measure is the median, over slow_rounds floods of flood_batches document batches, of the daemon's footprint growth (budget 1024 KB). Measured medians were 0-32 KB per flood with and without CPU load, against 320-448 KB for the earlier single-flood RSS measure. A build that keeps a slow client's whole backlog (QUEUE in crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs raised from 64 to 1<<20) was built but never measured: its first run stalled in macOS's assessment of new executables. That a kept backlog exceeds the budget is inferred from its size (5000 events with 160-character paths per flood), not observed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":827},"end":{"line":837},"content_hash":"be67e806b167263d6cedfacadd444a8750ddaa218457c63c4f32d442b666ac9e"},"suggested_fix":"Run scripts/perf-clients.py --quick once against that variant binary and confirm slow_growth_kb fails.","summary":"slow_growth_kb has not been shown to catch a kept backlog","supersedes":"2fae41b92c5d2a7666d11c3a6fb18f6e96b7466d6d9f7db468f0e8e22cfe2922","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/npm-ci-stamped.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:21:31.835008Z","id":"1bbd149ecbccd48cd976630f7121239641fe9b92fd8daef0106c6198c35cba74","body":{"detail":"web/ and plugins/pi/ moved to pnpm (scripts/pnpm-install-stamped.sh, pnpm-lock.yaml); crates/clax-worker kept npm and its package-lock.json, so this stamped npm ci stays for it alone (scripts/quality_gates.sh lane_worker, just worker-test). Moving it means a pnpm-lock.yaml for wrangler and its workerd and esbuild install scripts, which pnpm runs only when allowBuilds lists them (web/pnpm-workspace.yaml allows none), and an unchanged deploy path for crates/clax-worker/deploy.mjs and scripts/cloudflare-setup.sh, which run npm.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2},"end":{"line":3},"content_hash":"678ec3cbf9e49427879ba05b2fcb42a99778769e4fe186058dabbab2aa3ac421"},"summary":"crates/clax-worker installs with pnpm, as web/ and plugins/pi/ do","tags":["build","revisit:the Worker's packages come under Bazel, or npm leaves the machines that run the gates","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-wasm.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:35.311207Z","id":"93e0f83d91a850717ad4f58f21482ec4ec4b9bbc14fdb94652f95d2c10285326","body":{"detail":".github/workflows/ci.yml and rust-toolchain.toml add the wasm32-unknown-unknown target, and the script now also tries Debian and Ubuntu's /usr/lib/llvm-<N>/bin. Whether ubuntu-latest has a clang there that targets wasm32 beside an llvm-ar was not checked; the first CI run of the gates shows it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":30},"end":{"line":42},"content_hash":"e66b7d02889242a086cff19ef6e715715aeb07f55cc86dd9f77faecf1ca7e1c7"},"summary":"The wasm32 lane has run on macOS only: CI's Ubuntu LLVM is unverified","supersedes":"66e95d2ea22782cbc37390be298fd766ce5ef445f0e65031e13510713967d590","tags":["gates","ci","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:41:35.341823Z","id":"69fa4332dd9c3d30ee14a84f1597e6546f828db881567aabbc837c3938bfbdd7","body":{"detail":"They run first, alone, because several were timing-sensitive. Since 5da6c9a the view-mounting and child-process tests run under limits that end hangs only (MOUNT_TIMEOUT_MS 30 s, CHILD_TIMEOUT_MS 60 s, web/shell/src/test/timeouts.ts), so moving them into the lanes would save about 9 s of a gates run.","kind":"suggestion","ref":"git:e01d4166","span":{"start":{"line":162},"end":{"line":168},"content_hash":"82fe20109f02bee76696788391627a4839b255388a7a3efecad0187f317922f8"},"summary":"The shell's unit tests run alone (about 9 s); they may now join the lanes","supersedes":"0256afa979a18b3e310fc022b681eab3bb8d4f5157de3ae88f505bef6746877c","tags":["gate-speed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-crate-layers.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:52:20.537149Z","id":"904f8fe2617a660a7b40d8ce6a99608d286b2a72ba8c9ba0409327bf9486ffff","body":{"detail":"The layout's picture (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-workspace-layout-design.md section 2.1, lines 184-188) and ALLOWED here gain the crates the hosted work added: clax-rt (the runtime seam, tokio natively and a Worker's event loop on wasm32) depends on no workspace crate and every daemon crate uses it, so it joins clax-core's set; clax-git depends on nothing; clax-content-git on clax-core, clax-rt and clax-git. crates/clax-worker stays outside the workspace. This amends the decided layout spec, which is the owner's.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":31},"end":{"line":48},"content_hash":"8239201ac2a10212769d2e0e165229b85b50b75ec65a63159416546a23401147"},"summary":"Place clax-rt beside clax-core, clax-git on its own and clax-content-git over both in the layout","tags":["layout","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-clients.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:55:11.514108Z","id":"cede54937cd346ae19c60a8ab7e67c824d62cb677f6b17313455613849061ff3","body":{"detail":"The measure is the median, over slow_rounds floods of flood_batches document batches, of the daemon's footprint growth (budget 1024 KB). Measured medians were 0-32 KB per flood with and without CPU load, against 320-448 KB for the earlier single-flood RSS measure. A build that keeps a slow client's whole backlog (QUEUE in crates/clax-server/src/stream.rs raised from 64 to 1<<20) was built but never measured: its first run stalled in macOS's assessment of new executables. That a kept backlog exceeds the budget is inferred from its size (5000 events with 160-character paths per flood), not observed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":829},"end":{"line":839},"content_hash":"be67e806b167263d6cedfacadd444a8750ddaa218457c63c4f32d442b666ac9e"},"suggested_fix":"Run scripts/perf-clients.py --quick once against that variant binary and confirm slow_growth_kb fails.","summary":"slow_growth_kb has not been shown to catch a kept backlog","supersedes":"d5bf7790d56e2ef77e9188e4f838271a7fa7c2df25d43e72e2f571340e7ea94a","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:55:11.546191Z","id":"19ed076eac262bec12a035436c05705e62de550b5728608bfe916336fa552b44","body":{"detail":"test-repos.mjs needs jj (CLAX_TEST_JJ or jj on PATH) and fails without it; no gate installs one. After commit cfe9fdaa it passes with CLAX_TEST_JJ set (node test-repos.mjs --no-build: every check ok). The e2e lane's node e2e.mjs now publishes into git through the stand-in (REPO_STORE=memory) but does not clone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":140},"end":{"line":147},"content_hash":"b307cd78ca40244b0f066e84429c5be8f1d9fc44367795b203ac88b7d8c11c78"},"summary":"The worker lane does not run crates/clax-worker/test-repos.mjs (the RepoDO stand-in, /git/ clones and pushes, R2 assets)","supersedes":"b186353e057e2a4c353cbab7a1da788a980a4c83430c17d1f2d2dcb722ea6f3b","tags":["worker","gates","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/crate-package.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T03:22:35.072654Z","id":"54f2cebff7455dc8dd70dfaefffba283d87f7ff21b1166c392264ac987cb2e35","body":{"detail":"Not taken: it makes about eleven internal crates (clax-core, clax-store, clax-server, ...) public crates.io names that others can depend on, each release has to publish them in layer order with versioned path dependencies, and clax-embedded would still need its web UI, extension and plugins copied inside its own directory at publish time. The generated package keeps every internal crate private at the cost of rewriting paths (rewrite_sources, lines 211-232).","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":2},"end":{"line":38},"content_hash":"853c6518c8dbe0dbd3c800cd1bed9b5cb258f83c6d6ddd0c64245866ec5564fe"},"summary":"Publish every workspace crate to crates.io instead of one generated clax package","tags":["revisit:a workspace crate is wanted as a library on crates.io, or the path rewrite in scripts/crate-package.py breaks on a source pattern it cannot handle","session:claude-code:b2fe0abc-990b-4628-b4c7-4c6d7f3f261b"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/crate-package.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T03:22:35.110063Z","id":"24303270533236998727e5f7ca681eed8273d90551f9ca9be3237987f3c06117","body":{"detail":"rewrite_sources replaces every crate:: in a bundled library crate's sources with crate::<module>:: and every clax_<name>:: with crate::clax_<name>::, comments and string literals included. True of the sources at this commit (git grep finds none of these patterns in the eleven bundled crates' src/). A #[macro_export] macro would move to the package root and break its crate::<module>:: callers; a crate feature would be dropped (merged_dependencies refuses optional dependencies); a string such as a serde 'with = \"crate::x\"' is rewritten, which is right, but a log or error message quoting a path would change. tracing targets already read clax::clax_server::... in the package instead of clax_server::... . just crate-package (cargo check --locked of the packed crate) catches whatever does not compile.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":211},"end":{"line":232},"content_hash":"10cea40f7e1f818dfdb6c107a712446c3b8fb861b56b0d468eb7956b1cdb7ce0"},"summary":"The package's module rewrite is textual and assumes the bundled crates have no #[macro_export] macros, no extern crate, no crate features and no strings naming crate paths","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fe0abc-990b-4628-b4c7-4c6d7f3f261b"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:43:16.231572Z","id":"68efba6f9058766e3913758d626735c91e5cc05725d36bfc013a89029fdf4082","body":{"detail":"scripts/test-build-app-clax.sh checks scripts/build-app-clax.sh (the dry-run commands per platform and profile, and that place renames a binary into place rather than writing over it) in about a second, with no build. lane_scripts does not run it yet; add: run \"build app clax\" bash scripts/test-build-app-clax.sh","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":69},"end":{"line":75},"content_hash":"6cc1e1256a06c75d99f717cf75587dae4d3d430d62666bff5748f1b81bb179c4"},"suggested_fix":"Append `&& run \"build app clax\" scripts/test-build-app-clax.sh` to lane_scripts.","summary":"Add scripts/test-build-app-clax.sh to lane_scripts","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-clax.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:43:16.267329Z","id":"87888a6c851e5ee5685c4f01036464e501fb2d73299c977a5885e25f3de84ec2","body":{"detail":"build-app-clax.sh reads the NDK's linkers and llvm-strip from toolchains/llvm/prebuilt/darwin-x86_64/bin. On a Linux host (for example a CI runner) that directory is linux-x86_64, so the Android build fails there. macOS is the only host the app builds on today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"09b850f06c7cae12eeb8058727664f29cd3347bb06c6bdd77065659f4c45838e"},"suggested_fix":"Pick the prebuilt directory from `uname -s` (darwin-x86_64 or linux-x86_64) when a Linux host needs it.","summary":"The NDK toolchain path assumes a macOS host","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-clax.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:01:02.549258Z","id":"688a1a4ebb8462d93bf00159a978838a27eef14d5b16f26e7a891a1ed0598577","body":{"detail":"With --debug, cargo builds without --release, and crates/clax-server/src/routes/shell.rs:13-15 derives RustEmbed for ../../web/dist/ without rust-embed's debug-embed feature (Cargo.toml:35), so a debug binary reads web/dist from the build machine's checkout at run time instead of embedding it. Placed as jniLibs/<abi>/libclax.so by 'scripts/build-app-clax.sh android --debug', it runs on the device but every shell route finds no files. The script's header (lines 2-11) does not say this. A macOS --debug build works only while the checkout stays in place.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":37},"end":{"line":38},"content_hash":"9f90582cc8690f00ee4c05ffaf3820af8cc6e3cb2716f754e9ff450d083c9be4"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse --debug for android (or all), or say in the header and usage that a --debug build is host-only and not self-contained.","summary":"A --debug build places a clax that serves no web UI on Android","tags":["reviewer","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:31:23.489166Z","id":"e6390680abfd3b23f6337e0b7ad40d81a296cd8e3ab7cf3b9f88d467ee9d9b85","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fdd2f242","summary":"lane_scripts in scripts/quality_gates.sh now runs: run \"build app clax\" bash scripts/test-build-app-clax.sh. bash scripts/test-build-app-clax.sh prints only PASS lines and exits 0; bash -n scripts/quality_gates.sh passes.","supersedes":"68efba6f9058766e3913758d626735c91e5cc05725d36bfc013a89029fdf4082","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/quality_gates.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:09:51.141793Z","id":"f0a5abc048ba49efb42fd3215b891f5c0efd0880b3be711cf68d72684a19d264","body":{"detail":"They run first, alone, because several were timing-sensitive. Since 508ebe9 the view-mounting and child-process tests run under limits that end hangs only (MOUNT_TIMEOUT_MS 30 s, CHILD_TIMEOUT_MS 60 s, web/shell/src/test/timeouts.ts), so moving them into the lanes would save about 9 s of a gates run.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":153},"end":{"line":159},"content_hash":"43ba07359a2927073b8825eff55b3404c52ce0a02a6b7953d444a1c18c2256c6"},"summary":"The shell's unit tests run alone (about 9 s); they may now join the lanes","supersedes":"39562e1125375035c0a8ea3214e707f7ee268df5e36d450a5c361549026fe126","tags":["gate-speed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-home-bundle.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:54:52.511668Z","id":"a58f4ba9d767c7e1ec9f1a6b575b672ae20c1443b3aa8d62cab5eedb8918d3d0","body":{"detail":"Why this key: lib/bundle/trust.dart decide() matches an installed app to a bundle by lineage AND author key, so every shipped release must carry the same key or installs treat it as a foreign lineage (no silent update, spec 2026-10-16-home-screen-app-design §5). A key committed to the repository would let anyone sign a bundle on the home lineage that installs accept as an update of the home app, which holds the home capability; this install's own BundleKey (lib/platform/bundle_key.dart) differs per device, so it cannot sign a shared release. The public key is recorded in apps/clax_app/assets/home/release.json (key) and tool/pack_home.dart refuses to pack with any other key or to mint a new one once that record exists. Accepted risk: losing the seed file means the next release cannot be signed as the same lineage; back it up (for example into 1Password, as scripts/pack-extension.sh does for the extension key) and restore it to the same path or CLAX_HOME_BUNDLE_KEY before packing.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":10},"end":{"line":27},"content_hash":"a684ed3d4ac165c88b36bd806663fcc26658e09d9b5b34d9e5d693ed1e92e26e"},"summary":"The shipped home app (apps/clax_app/assets/home/home.clax) is signed by a dedicated build-time Ed25519 key whose only copy is the seed file ~/.config/clax/home-bundle/key on the machine that packed it","tags":["signing","home-app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-clax.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:00:08.329118Z","id":"4730c5a245dc7ea03f3d9e05f3bafacc837bac5d58489ceef93466e0fc127b20","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"688a1a4ebb8462d93bf00159a978838a27eef14d5b16f26e7a891a1ed0598577","summary":"With Bazel the app's Android clax is //crates/clax-cli:clax_android_{arm64,x86_64}, always optimized and with the web UI embedded (bazel/android/clax.bzl), so this applies to the native build only (just app-clax-native android --debug).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-clax.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:00:08.329249Z","id":"695b9dc7e307a074d06d228f5e4c7c7c91b81fd1faee3815ee9f901b2372bff7","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"87888a6c851e5ee5685c4f01036464e501fb2d73299c977a5885e25f3de84ec2","summary":"With Bazel the NDK is fetched for the host by checksum, darwin or linux (android_ndk.configure in MODULE.bazel, bazel/android/rules_android_ndk.patch), so this applies to the native build only (just app-clax-native).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-home-bundle.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:27:16.237824Z","id":"83589be0d380e9ff8d385fad46591c375b7098377e8a1636629f6d69d687cb93","body":{"detail":"Why this key: lib/bundle/trust.dart decide() matches an installed app to a bundle by lineage AND author key, so every shipped release must carry the same key or installs treat it as a foreign lineage (no silent update). A key committed to the repository would let anyone sign a bundle on the home lineage that installs accept as an update of the home app, which holds the home capability; this install's own BundleKey (lib/platform/bundle_key.dart) differs per device, so it cannot sign a shared release. The public key is pinned as `key` in apps/clax_app/home/manifest.json, and tool/pack_home.dart (127-141) refuses to pack a release with any other key. Accepted risk: losing the seed file means the next release cannot be signed as the same lineage, and losing the ledger beside it (`releases`, tool/home-version.sh) restarts versions at the manifest's `version` + 1; back the directory up (for example into 1Password, as scripts/pack-extension.sh does for the extension key) and restore it to the same path or CLAX_HOME_BUNDLE_KEY before building.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":14},"end":{"line":22},"content_hash":"ce3fa6a1e9259d39bcd62faa6aae1e49aed8fe829555bd74ed272d87c846933e"},"summary":"The shipped home app (assets/home/home.clax, built by //apps/clax_app:home_bundle and this script) is signed by a dedicated build-time Ed25519 key whose only copy is the seed file ~/.config/clax/home-bundle/key on the machine that releases it","supersedes":"a58f4ba9d767c7e1ec9f1a6b575b672ae20c1443b3aa8d62cab5eedb8918d3d0","tags":["signing","home-app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-ios-spawns.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T04:59:32.393903Z","id":"3b20d204f41fa4f90a613de126e38f783a5c2ad964e33ea5af572f6b86c1806f","body":{"detail":"scripts/ios-spawns.allow names a file and function per launch (crates/clax-core/src/gitctx.rs spawn, remote.rs process_started, clax-mcp channel.rs process_argv, tools.rs run_opener, clax-realtime push.rs run_queue); a new launch added to one of those functions, or a gate removed from one, passes. Whether the iOS arms compile is the job of a build of the daemon for aarch64-apple-ios (cargo check --target aarch64-apple-ios -p clax-server -p clax-mcp passes at a6b26d896); whether they run nothing is reviewed per entry.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":54},"content_hash":"60ee3370d19e137bf7fee95f6ee65ab9988001ad220c8d9f2e36fa8ae30b0731"},"summary":"An allowed launch is trusted by its function name: the check does not read the cfg that keeps it off on iOS","tags":["revisit:a launch reaches iOS through an allowed function","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/sync-tokens.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:08:15.982316Z","id":"519517dd7c79fd92bbef52364f24c2463ecaaf79978e494b12da853958a9723c","body":{"detail":"kit_css rewrites only the text between tokens:begin and tokens:end, and kit_unguarded_mixes looks only for color-mix outside @supports. A later `:root { --k-bg: #fff }` below tokens:end wins by source order and --check still passes. design/tokens.json's contrast pairs also run only on the base palettes, never lightMore/darkMore (harmless while only border differs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":549},"end":{"line":583},"content_hash":"e7d7d1a902fa3cdf126a050ae808cdb277973cbcdbf5e4349971e0d1580278ba"},"suggested_fix":"Fail --check when a name in tokens.json's kit map is declared outside the region (allowing the documented --k-accent-soft @supports override).","summary":"The sync check does not notice a mapped --k-* token re-declared outside kit.css's markers, which silently overrides the brand","tags":["review","ui-phase-1","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:09:36.137449Z","id":"44eecbbca2a89a4cd27c706402f4bc0e670d126f73f208aab6d00192de130304","body":{"detail":"scripts/check-no-unsafe.sh checks only the manifests and sources in its runfiles, and these two lists are written by hand. A new crate (crates/clax-ios included) that is not added to both passes //scripts:no_unsafe whatever it contains; only the native run (scripts/quality_gates.sh, which scans the checkout) sees it. scripts/bazel-sync.sh --check already fails on a crate without a BUILD.bazel; it could also fail on a crate absent from these lists, or the lists could be derived into bazel/workspace.bzl.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":76},"end":{"line":114},"content_hash":"1ccfcbf85f3d87164ea47ab017fa65cb482a58daf98f95cfb9ed960d36b23f95"},"summary":"A crate missing from RUST_SOURCES and CRATE_MANIFESTS is invisible to //scripts:no_unsafe under Bazel","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:16:43.345390Z","id":"a98b1e2b13980f2cbbff11615c0589b37ee475e81706669fe1b9754807cfaac1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:dbd027242","summary":"Fixed: clax-ios is in RUST_SOURCES and CRATE_MANIFESTS (scripts/BUILD.bazel), so the Bazel check reads its manifest and sources; bazelisk test //scripts:no_unsafe //scripts:crate_layers //scripts:ios_spawns: 3 PASSED, with crates/clax-ios/src/lib.rs's four exports present","supersedes":"44eecbbca2a89a4cd27c706402f4bc0e670d126f73f208aab6d00192de130304","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-ios-spawns.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:43:36.758751Z","id":"7127a859cf0aae4da24aab12bfd2305216effcf8f6e74531c579e6c726b0490b","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3b20d204f41fa4f90a613de126e38f783a5c2ad964e33ea5af572f6b86c1806f","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":54},"content_hash":"60ee3370d19e137bf7fee95f6ee65ab9988001ad220c8d9f2e36fa8ae30b0731"},"summary":"The iOS arms now compile under Bazel in the test suite: //crates/clax-ios:ios_build_test builds clax-ios and its dependencies (clax-server, clax-mcp, clax-core, clax-realtime) for aarch64-apple-ios and aarch64-apple-ios-sim (bazelisk test //crates/clax-ios:ios_build_test: PASSED at 02fd07054). Whether an allowed function runs nothing on iOS is still reviewed per entry.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-icons.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:44:20.267870Z","id":"aa0964b2abd3eb224e13c213ad2961bd29a44b7ad24990de4d89635fa1cca8e0","body":{"detail":"rules_flutter's flutter_macos_app (apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel :macos_app) defaults app_icons to macos/Runner/Assets.xcassets/AppIcon.appiconset and rules_apple refuses an .appiconset and a .icon together; the Xcode native twin does not list macos/Runner/AppIcon.icon in macos/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj. So macOS 26 shows the appiconset's light PNGs, with no dark or tinted appearance. actool from Xcode 26.6 compiles AppIcon.icon alone at --minimum-deployment-target 12.0 into Assets.car and an AppIcon.icns fallback (xcrun actool --compile OUT --platform macosx --minimum-deployment-target 12.0 --app-icon AppIcon … AppIcon.icon), so passing app_icons = glob([\"macos/Runner/AppIcon.icon/**\"]) and adding the bundle to the Xcode project could ship it to every supported macOS, at the cost of 12–15 drawing the system's fallback rather than the appiconset's shadowed body. Which icon source macOS builds ship is the owner's call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":363},"end":{"line":415},"content_hash":"67a50b0ac3f9d545a83e9aca334b0d1f12dc71e19fca728cb223088d4849c0ef"},"summary":"AppIcon.icon is rendered and committed, but neither build ships it","tags":["status:needs-decision","revisit:macOS dark or tinted app icons wanted","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-icons.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:00:02.013360Z","id":"aef420802d9b9985f3b545562f90677ca5ab530f7f3217a22ee5f11b38a03f8f","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/android/app/src/main/res/drawable/splash_mark.xml carries design/mark.json's paths scaled to 132 dp on a 288 dp canvas, and res/values/clax_colors.xml and values-night/clax_colors.xml carry tokens.json's bg, you, agent and fg. TARGETS here does not write them and --check (//design:icons_sync) does not cover them, so a changed mark or token updates the icons and ClaxSplash but leaves the splash stale.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":419},"end":{"line":419},"content_hash":"3054ea691a777a173857add059250d5c4f3a2038f5e2160868e6047c9edfc050"},"suggested_fix":"Add a splash target to TARGETS that writes splash_mark.xml and both clax_colors.xml with the GENERATED header, so --check covers them.","summary":"The Android splash's mark and colours are copied by hand, not rendered from design/mark.json and design/tokens.json","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/sync-tokens.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:13:52.253603Z","id":"eaffb9abc1b66c04f53e11230a900f40eec6bf51f3b47a441c65b1fcc63c2286","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:448da8e65","summary":"kit_redeclared fails a mapped --k-* declared outside the region and outside @supports, and contrast pairs run on the more-contrast palettes. Cases 13 and 16 of scripts/test-sync-tokens.sh: `bazelisk test //scripts:sync_tokens //design:tokens_sync` PASSED.","supersedes":"519517dd7c79fd92bbef52364f24c2463ecaaf79978e494b12da853958a9723c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-copy.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:21:34.315462Z","id":"31e0a7591c99f643f99d2a1550f467c4ca5065534d122e5ebf21512b1842aafc","body":{"detail":"So htm attributes (title=\"Nothing here\"), JSON in a literal and CSS or regex text mostly pass without an allow comment, at the cost that a quoted phrase right after other punctuation (—\"word\", /\"word\") passes unchecked. Apostrophes, three dots and raw errors are not heuristic in this way.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":41},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"2d529250efa58294284943b50756999ca2a4a62962492103df1fc052f7a1ee4b"},"summary":"The straight-quotes rule is a heuristic: it counts a \" or ' only after the literal's start, a space or a bracket, and skips literals that open with { or [","tags":["copy","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-icons.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:31:00.126540Z","id":"2ae8e8b71d248b34c8470dd058aff71e62e5e8b8f55ecf905fdd55eb0b239330","body":{"detail":"app_icon_16.png is apple_svg(16, 'light'): the 560-in-1024 mark becomes about 9 px wide, so the 1.7-radius dot and the 2.6 stroke arcs share pixels (target/flutter-app/shots/icons/mac-light-16-nn.png). Finder's list view, Spotlight and the Dock's small sizes show this one. Android's mdpi 48 px legacy icon still separates the three shapes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":348},"end":{"line":351},"content_hash":"94455d049bd50c032a30ace16611e598d81c7e8fd9147f56efc9808cc30dfea8"},"suggested_fix":"Draw the 16 px slot (and check 32) with a small-size variant (larger mark in the body, the dot and the gaps snapped to whole pixels), or check them on a Mac and record the call.","summary":"The 16 px macOS icon is the 1024 design scaled down: the dot fuses with both arcs into a grey bar and the mark reads as “>-<”","tags":["review","icons","phase-2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-icons.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:46:02.697958Z","id":"feaee7aa4da11868248eb5458a1f824abc5f9922ad9570b6d8d10bc998ade399","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:541bbce99","summary":"Fixed: APPLE_SMALL draws app_icon_16.png and app_icon_32.png with a 704/640-wide mark of shallower arcs, a stroke of 3 and a dot of radius 2, about 1.5 px between each arc and the dot at 16 px. scripts/build-app-icons.sh --preview renders mac-{light,dark}-{16,32,64}.png: arc, gap, dot, gap, arc in both themes; bazelisk test //design:icons_sync passes.","supersedes":"2ae8e8b71d248b34c8470dd058aff71e62e5e8b8f55ecf905fdd55eb0b239330","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/app-iphone.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:42:12.189672Z","id":"66eb869f11677352b02c0309b9f7e702dfa1f1dba63242ebacbf416ca10745aa","body":{"detail":"No signing inputs, device or App Store Connect key exist on this machine yet, so these steps were never run for real. The command shapes come from Xcode 26.6's own help: altool 26.40.1 documents `--upload-package <ipa> --api-key <ID> --api-issuer <ID>` (no `--type`; the legacy `--apiKey`/`--apiIssuer` spelling is behind `--use-old-altool`), and `devicectl device info files` only lists a container, so daemon.json is read with `devicectl device copy from --domain-type appDataContainer`. The launched PID is read from `devicectl device process launch --json-output` at result.process.processIdentifier, and devices from `devicectl list devices --json-output` (hardwareProperties.platform, connectionProperties.pairingState and tunnelState), key paths not yet seen on a real device's output.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":284},"end":{"line":351},"content_hash":"f417eeba9adf4f4a2f23290504679c72de20b83be6fe4781ac9487f19d4fa4f4"},"suggested_fix":"On the first device build and the first TestFlight upload, run scripts/app-iphone.sh (dry run, then --i-know-what-i-am-doing) and fix any key path or flag that differs; then resolve this.","summary":"The device install, launch and daemon.json read, and the altool upload, have run only against the stubs of scripts/test-app-iphone.sh","tags":["ios","testflight","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-no-unsafe.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:42:06.460474Z","id":"e2012d4a41ccdfc5636abd6f5b0d2b52ef6f9e3f2d4539898428cea223bb8a01","body":{"detail":"Two shapes pass the check (scripts/check-no-unsafe.sh run on a copy of Cargo.toml, crates/clax-embed/Cargo.toml and crates/clax-embed/src/ffi.rs, exit 0 for each): (1) in the body of `pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn clax_embed_open`, a line `let _b = Box::from_raw(home.as_ptr() as *mut [u8; 4]);` with no unsafe block. Edition 2024 makes `unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn` a warning, not an error (`rustc --edition 2024` on such a function prints `warning[E0133]: call to unsafe function ... requires unsafe block` and exits 0), and the crate's lint flags (bazel/workspace.bzl crates/clax-embed lint_flags, crates/clax-embed/Cargo.toml [lints.rust]) do not deny it; the script only looks for lines with the word `unsafe`. (2) `pub extern \"C\" fn clax_embed_close(core: u64) -> i32 { unsafe { *(core as *mut u8) = 0 }; crate::ffi_close(core) }` on one line: the whole signature line ($i + 1) is granted. scripts/test-check-no-unsafe.sh even has a passing case \"an export on one line\". Today clippy's -Dwarnings (`--config=clippy` in scripts/bazel-test.sh) catches (1) and the rustfmt check catches (2), so `just ci` holds, but spec 2026-10-19 §14 says //scripts:no_unsafe itself fails on any other unsafe, a second from_raw_parts and Box::from_raw.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":123},"end":{"line":146},"content_hash":"d2bc47a735b12808f77405876e2ddd24e46f9df99c51479618c63a6715bb7937"},"suggested_fix":"Add `unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn = \"forbid\"` to crates/clax-embed/Cargo.toml [lints.rust] (and -Funsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn to its lint_flags via just bazel-sync), have the check require it, and grant only a signature line that ends at its `(` or `{` (nothing after the opening brace); add both shapes as failing cases in scripts/test-check-no-unsafe.sh.","summary":"//scripts:no_unsafe passes an unsafe operation in clax-embed's exports that carries no `unsafe` keyword, and any code on a granted signature line","tags":["review","unsafe","embed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-no-unsafe.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:32:05.111159Z","id":"648316b6f4666607ccb562023ca0f12ad76fcb4991b978f6dcaf82531a68c2f1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b0e7f48e9","summary":"Fixed in b0e7f48e9: crates/clax-embed/Cargo.toml forbids unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn (bazel/workspace.bzl lint_flags -Funsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn), the check fails without it, and a signature line is granted only up to its `(`. //scripts:no_unsafe_test passes with the new cases 'unsafe after the brace of an export on one line', 'unsafe after the brace of a signature line', 'an unsafe operation with no unsafe block, the lint not forbidden' and 'clax-embed only denying unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn', all of which failed against the old check; `rustc --edition 2024 -Funsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn` on Box::from_raw in an unsafe fn body now errors E0133.","supersedes":"e2012d4a41ccdfc5636abd6f5b0d2b52ef6f9e3f2d4539898428cea223bb8a01","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/patch-pub.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:39:08.878040Z","id":"3d901cf2ba8e71090d93ab5d0c9271d623e6611d0d71097365b936cf824d1b3e","body":{"detail":"Only its dry run was run. scripts/run.sh's native app-integration and app-macos run it, then flutter with PUB_CACHE at that directory; whether flutter pub get --enforce-lockfile leaves pubspec.lock unchanged with a private PUB_CACHE, and whether the native macOS build compiles the patched plugin, are unverified.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":24},"end":{"line":66},"content_hash":"6289bfde1e17533e4f8005d4c524b092cdbf33ed2ff4e2f3dac28fd63832ee14"},"summary":"patch-pub.sh's acting run (flutter pub get into apps/clax_app/build-native/pub-cache, then the patch) has not been run, nor the native recipes that call it","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/app-android-emulator.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:18:26.371055Z","id":"5abbf5a5856d48ac87240afb0b5c876b5037b0a6838fb2d9c3b208805b878c9f","body":{"detail":"target/android-avd/Clax_Pixel.running keeps only the serial and PID. If the emulator dies without --stop (a crash, a reboot, a test killed by Bazel's timeout) and the PID is later reused, running_one reports that process; --start prints 'already running' with its PID, and --stop sends adb emu kill (no effect), waits up to 60 s while the process lives, then kill PID (lines 269-275).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":176},"end":{"line":182},"content_hash":"b2e09b9a96c4ea25bb2e58719bdd767fadc9cc6cc9b8f685ded0687436b5faad"},"suggested_fix":"Write the process's start time and command (ps -o lstart= -o comm= -p PID) beside the PID at start, and have running_one compare both before reporting or stopping; otherwise remove the file and report nothing running.","summary":"The emulator's PID is trusted by kill -0 alone: a stale .running file and a reused PID make --start report a stranger as the emulator and --stop kill it after 60 s","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/app-android-emulator.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:18:26.371085Z","id":"31561f1121a4b35b580d3d41fdcc408ed33410559201aed58cd8f83e2e11e081","body":{"detail":"The early-exit branch (lines 231-236) removes the .running file but never runs adb kill-server on ANDROID_ADB_SERVER_PORT, so an adb server of this script outlives it. There is no trap, so SIGINT or SIGTERM during the boot wait leaves the backgrounded emulator and its adb server running with no record of who owns them once .running is stale. A private adb server still enumerates USB devices, so whether it contends with the owner's adb on 5037 for a plugged-in phone is unverified.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":216},"end":{"line":248},"content_hash":"a409225ba847869cdd01ae909bb0ae4fd54adf56418fb5593ea9aa43c2d1d5f0"},"suggested_fix":"trap on EXIT/INT/TERM in --start that, unless boot succeeded, stops the PID it started and runs adb kill-server on its port; verify with a phone plugged in that adb -P 5037 devices keeps it 'device' while the emulator runs.","summary":"--start cleans up only on its 300 s timeout: an emulator that exits while booting leaves its adb server on port+10000, and an interrupt during the wait leaves the emulator running","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/app-android-emulator.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:18:26.371111Z","id":"c0e0d9f797ba3393cce36adf41e7a06641f838153db0074c7432416b4b1bafd1","body":{"detail":"fastboot.forceColdBoot=yes, -no-snapshot and tool/android-integration-run.sh's uninstall before each install mean no run reuses the AVD's data, yet target/android-avd/Clax_Pixel.avd/userdata-qemu.img.qcow2 was 1.3 GB here, per worktree, up to the 6G data partition. The system image is shared: Bazel 9.3's repository contents cache links external/+http_archive+android_system_image into ~/Library/Caches/bazel/_bazel_alex/cache/repos/v1/contents (4.3 GB unpacked, once per user, plus its 1.7 GB zip in content_addressable), so docs/bazel.md's 'unpacks the system image into the output base' overstates the per-worktree cost.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":141},"end":{"line":163},"content_hash":"94fd14d0fce85130f34d4f4d3c14155f341fef3552eb6c676e5c941527260bfd"},"suggested_fix":"Boot with -read-only (writes go to temporary files removed at exit, so the AVD neither grows nor locks, and runs in two worktrees could share one AVD); add --clean that removes target/android-avd, target/android-home and target/android-sdk; correct docs/bazel.md's disk note.","summary":"Each worktree's AVD keeps a writable data image that grows (1.3 GB in this worktree after one run) though nothing in it is reused","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/app-macos-dev.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:18:26.371136Z","id":"67b692abc6583acd375a8de32b532ba314b3c0559b3787b50642692397dd94d4","body":{"detail":"apps/clax_app/macos/Runner/SchemeHost.swift sets FWFWebViewFlutterWKWebViewExternalAPI.configurationHook, which only configuration-hook.patch adds. scripts/run.sh's native app-integration and app-macos run scripts/patch-pub.sh and set PUB_CACHE to apps/clax_app/build-native/pub-cache; app-macos-dev.sh (the hot-reload loop, docs/usage.md:715) does neither.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":44},"content_hash":"054c9ceeaff81fddc73e1a604ba9cae06fe9cf77d172618290f729c6cddb4b80"},"suggested_fix":"Run ./scripts/patch-pub.sh --i-know-what-i-am-doing in app-macos-dev.sh's steps and exec flutter run with PUB_CACHE at that directory, and list the step in its dry run.","summary":"just app-macos-dev runs flutter run with the unpatched webview_flutter_wkwebview, which has no configurationHook, so the Mac runner no longer compiles there","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:07:20.175030Z","id":"42a67fae7d355b48ccdcd7e2fc49aef86d4b4601a6ee97489da7e7e1f617736d","body":{"detail":"//apps/clax_app:macos_app at 79cecdcc6, launched with a scratch CLAX_APP_DIR: a sample of the app showed its flutter_secure_storage queue in SecItemCopyMatching -> SecKeychainItemCopyContent for the whole run, ioreg reported CGSSessionScreenIsLocked = Yes, the daemon was never spawned and no timings.jsonl was written. scripts/perf-app-launch.sh --macos --runs 1 --i-know-what-i-am-doing reported both launches missing (60 s cap each), stopped each app by PID and removed its scratch directory. The --android path (lines 266-313) has not run against a device or emulator either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":44},"end":{"line":47},"content_hash":"e29ac5cd957152be85b7473e1e7fc9c97776068ce8f69d0ff8decb6170d348d6"},"suggested_fix":"With the screen unlocked: CLAX_PERF_JSON=target/perf/app-launch-before.json scripts/perf-app-launch.sh --macos --record --i-know-what-i-am-doing, answering Always Allow on the first launch's keychain prompt; then scripts/perf-log.sh record target/perf/app-launch-before.json, and commit web/perf/budget.json. On the phone, with its owner present, the same with --android after just app-phone.","summary":"No launch baseline is recorded and web/perf/budget.json has no app_home_usable_ms or app_home_cover_ms budget: every macOS launch of the ad hoc signed daemon build waited on the login keychain prompt for the saved API key while the screen was locked","tags":["time-to-usable","needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:18:11.920109Z","id":"f729ccc3cbe0db5380c388921f1fced9153dd0382f7384e0fb064750e22ed66d","body":{"detail":"Failure: scripts/perf-app-launch.sh --macos --i-know-what-i-am-doing on a real build (or --android). The macOS loop SIGTERMs the app as soon as the count of home-usable lines grows (lines 236-244); the Android loop force-stops it at the next iteration's start (line 296) right after the same check. HomeSnapshotter takes the snapshot only 3 s after a shown load (apps/clax_app/lib/home/home_snapshot.dart:262 settle, updated() at 310-317) or when home is covered or put in the background; SIGTERM and am force-stop run neither. The scratch CLAX_APP_DIR is new on each script run, so <dir>/cache/home/home-snapshot.bin never exists: every launch takes the no-snapshot path, home-cover is never written, the JSON reports app_home_cover_ms runs 0 with missing equal to the run count, --record writes no cover budget, and the dropped launch drops nothing that differs from the others. docs/usage.md (\"Measuring the home screen's start\") itself says to leave the home screen up for a second before the next launch. The fake app in scripts/test-perf-app-launch.sh:96-120 writes home-cover from a script, so the test passes regardless.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":231},"end":{"line":245},"content_hash":"01647a0a64d1d224c1553d0bb1087531679fe774f7b6b966f4555d46b39a0b6c"},"suggested_fix":"After the dropped launch's home-usable, wait (a bounded loop on the condition, e.g. 30 s) for <scratch>/cache/home/home-snapshot.bin to exist before stopping the app, and stop the run with a message if it never appears; on Android the same with `run-as dev.empathic.clax ls cache/home/home-snapshot.bin`. Make the fake app write home-cover only when a snapshot file exists and write that file a moment after home-usable, so the test fails on the current loop.","summary":"Each launch is stopped the moment home-usable is written, before the home screen's snapshot is taken, so no launch ever has a snapshot: app_home_cover_ms is never measured and every home-usable is a launch without its cover","tags":["review","time-to-usable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:18:11.920218Z","id":"f8e77ca85d183cc41ea0defc352026e3dd581ab3af4e9bccd9d9f335cd5dfc6d","body":{"detail":"CLAX_APP_DIR (apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart:104-117) moves only the support and cache directories. The executable runs as dev.empathic.clax, so everything else lands in ~/Library/Containers/dev.empathic.clax/Data, the container of the owner's installed app: AppKit's frame autosave rewrites 'NSWindow Frame ClaxMain' in Data/Library/Preferences/dev.empathic.clax.plist (on this Mac that file was last written at 06:53 on 2026-10-20, when Data/Library/Caches/flutter_engine was also made); once a launch reaches the home screen, WKWebView keeps localStorage, IndexedDB and the clax_key_<port> cookie of each scratch daemon's origins (http://127.0.0.1:<port>, http://<id>.localhost:<port>) in the container's default website data store, which the owner's app shares, and a scratch port that equals the installed app's kept port (its daemon-port, 57053 on this Mac, when that app is not running) shares an origin with the owner's pages. Answering Always Allow adds the measured build's ad hoc signature to the ACL of the owner's saved API key (flutter_secure_storage, login keychain: apps/clax_app/lib/platform/secure_key.dart), and that build reads the real key. Restoring the plist afterwards is unreliable while cfprefsd caches it and the installed app may be running.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":191},"end":{"line":233},"content_hash":"7aca189c46c14623130fac1d9e099f121c56a239b8e417d23475cea8d2815cfb"},"suggested_fix":"Unpack the measured app, set CFBundleIdentifier to dev.empathic.clax.perf in its Info.plist and re-sign the outer bundle ad hoc keeping its entitlements (codesign --force --sign - --preserve-metadata=entitlements,flags,runtime, without identifier), so it runs in a container of its own that the script deletes at the end; check first that the sandbox names the container by the new identifier. The keychain ACL write stays (the item is the owner's), unless the measured run is given no key. The owner decides whether a re-identified copy is a faithful measure.","summary":"A measured macOS run writes into the owner's own app container: the window frame default, WebKit website data and cookies, Flutter's engine cache, and on Always Allow the keychain item's ACL","tags":["review","time-to-usable","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:18:11.920261Z","id":"8c98876b6e103519553d2fe0c008cfe0e74f81577858f1136db9bd08ad97ac5a","body":{"detail":"With the screen locked or a keychain prompt waiting, every launch waits out the cap: `just perf` on a Mac (scripts/run.sh _perf_app_launch) then spends about (N+1) x 60 s, 10 minutes at the default 9, to report nothing. When only some launches are missing, `missing` appears in the stdout JSON (line 121) but not in the CLAX_PERF_JSON lines (lines 128-136), and --record (lines 142-154) writes a budget from however many launches finished, which is then never rewritten (--record skips a platform's existing budgets).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":236},"end":{"line":243},"content_hash":"cfd6daefd9153a0161ebb6435ad08e4a9092a43c7d450238d7b5fb19ab80f6d9"},"suggested_fix":"Stop after the dropped launch when it gives no home-usable (a lock or a prompt does not clear by itself), and check ioreg's CGSSessionScreenIsLocked before the first launch; refuse --record when app_home_usable_ms.missing or app_home_cover_ms.missing is above 0; write the missing count as its own perf-log line.","summary":"A launch that times out costs its full 60 s and the run goes on, and the summary, the perf-log lines and --record treat a partial run like a full one","tags":["review","time-to-usable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:18:11.920293Z","id":"f595e91d68eb4e37f90fdb7eedf76158710dfb00fe1fd21d20ecade5f7d04584","body":{"detail":"The summary (lines 116-155) names only the platform. scripts/perf-log.sh record stamps `git rev-parse HEAD` of the checkout it runs in (scripts/perf-log.sh:39-40, PERF_COMMIT set there, overriding any value in the environment). The daemon baseline that spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md section 12 asks for has to come from a build before the core lands, measured with this script's --app from a later checkout, so its perf-log record names the wrong commit, and the app's clax reports clax_commit 'unknown' (the fixture's audit rows, crates/clax-embed/tests/fixtures/homes/flutter-app-43.sql:302-317), so the build cannot tell either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":209},"end":{"line":225},"content_hash":"4793510c7101664f4f30934486d04c8a6176af0ae363ddd9a3fd76e73bbd3c1e"},"suggested_fix":"Add an \"app\" object to the JSON (the bundle path, the zip's sha256 that line 215 already computes, and the bundle's CFBundleVersion) and a --commit <sha> label written into each perf-log line's name or a field; let scripts/perf-log.sh record take PERF_COMMIT from the environment when set.","summary":"Nothing records which build was measured: with --app, the figures and scripts/perf-log.sh's record are attributed to the checkout's HEAD, not to the app","tags":["review","time-to-usable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:18:11.920326Z","id":"76129aca76494b5d10b4a802df78628eb12ad8704277fc8fa46ed4601641233c","body":{"detail":"--record writes all_budgets[platform] = {\"app_home_usable_ms\": …, \"app_home_cover_ms\": …}. usable.perf.ts keys the same file by `${platform()}-${arch()}` and treats any entry as its Budget: judge() takes `b = all[PLATFORM] ?? null` (line 318), so b is no longer null, its 'no baseline, report only' branch is skipped, and b.baseline[mode] (line 324) or b.control[mode] (line 346) throws a TypeError. Only darwin-arm64 has a web entry today, so an Intel Mac (darwin-x64) is the case; Android keys (android-<model>) never match Node's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":142},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"2a6d079174cd789a9e65ee5e6e574635582d813f7573723d54b6ddfc4b9d59ed"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the app's budgets apart from the web ones (a top-level \"app\" object keyed by platform, or web/perf/app-budget.json), or have usable.perf.ts treat an entry without `baseline` as no budget.","summary":"--record on a platform with no web budget makes an entry that web/perf/usable.perf.ts then reads as a full Budget and fails on","tags":["review","time-to-usable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:18:11.920985Z","id":"7d49f12ad45500df26366798af0aedb3b9c33c060669df84dcce3ec707fa9cba","body":{"detail":"(1) `scripts/perf-log.sh record <metrics>` only prints the record; `--append target/perf-log.jsonl` keeps it (scripts/perf-log.sh:7-11), and the record names the checkout's HEAD, so run it from a checkout of the measured build's commit. (2) The macOS measure can be taken after the core lands from a build of the parent of the commit that puts the app on the core: build //apps/clax_app:macos_app at that commit from a clean checkout, keep its zip under target/perf/, and run this script from the current checkout with --app <zip> (the zip is unpacked once by content under target/perf/app-<sha12>, and its ad hoc signature stays the same, so one Always Allow serves every run of it). The snapshot blocker on lines 231-245 of this script has to be fixed first or app_home_cover_ms comes out empty. (3) This branch's build carries migrations past the installed homes' 43 (crates/clax-embed/tests/old_homes.rs asserts the open ends at JOBS_MIGRATION, 46), and spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md section 10.2 forbids installing such a build on the owner's devices before the last task copies and checks their homes. --android measures the installed app against the phone's real home, so the phone's daemon baseline is the build installed now, measured without `just app-phone`.","kind":"comment","references":"42a67fae7d355b48ccdcd7e2fc49aef86d4b4601a6ee97489da7e7e1f617736d","summary":"The baseline's procedure needs three corrections: append to the perf log with --append, measure the daemon build with --app after the core lands, and take the phone's baseline on the installed build without just app-phone","tags":["review","time-to-usable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:41:03.074244Z","id":"30b78596a6d5011566bd47ba07c4ce4c542886979089bb577affc6979907011b","body":{"detail":"Checked on 2026-10-20 with the screen locked: target/perf/app-ebea9c8c387b/Clax.app copied with ditto, CFBundleIdentifier set to dev.empathic.clax.perf, signed with codesign --force --sign - --preserve-metadata=entitlements,flags,runtime (codesign -dv: Identifier=dev.empathic.clax.perf, Signature=adhoc, app-sandbox kept; codesign --verify --deep --strict passed). Launched once by its Contents/MacOS/Clax: the sandbox made ~/Library/Containers/dev.empathic.clax.perf within 1.5 s, with Data/Library/Application Support/dev.empathic.clax.perf (install-id, clax-home/config.toml) and Data/Library/Caches/dev.empathic.clax.perf and flutter_engine; ~/Library/Containers/dev.empathic.clax/Data/Library/Preferences/dev.empathic.clax.plist kept its mtime. A sample of the copy showed its main work in SecItemCopyMatching -> SecKeychainItemCopyContent, as record 42a67fae saw for the dev.empathic.clax build: flutter_secure_storage_darwin 0.4.3 queries the login keychain (usesDataProtectionKeychain false, apps/clax_app/lib/platform/secure_key.dart) by service flutter_secure_storage_service and account anthropic_api_key, with no bundle ID in the query, so the copy matches the item the installed app saved and macOS asks whether to let it read it. No timings.jsonl and no daemon: DaemonSupervisor starts the daemon only after apiKey() returns (apps/clax_app/lib/daemon/supervisor.dart _keyOrNull). The copy was stopped by its PID and its container removed. Without a saved key the read returns null at once and the daemon starts with sample() off (_keyOrNull; nothing else on the way to the home screen needs the key), so home-usable would be written: the measure needs the copy to read no key, not a key. The scripted agent mode (--dart-define=CLAX_SCRIPTED_AGENT, lib/main.dart:54-59) is no way round: it is debug-only and replaces only the agent backend, while the supervisor still reads secureKey.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":27},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"ef00e59479f29f8fa1f9ccbb53956e2121ab6f907df48da58385f672d22e5bcc"},"suggested_fix":"Options for the owner: (a) the app reads no key when its environment says so, e.g. CLAX_APP_NO_KEY=1 making main.dart's secureKey a store with no key, set by scripts/perf-app-launch.sh; the daemon baseline then needs that change on the pre-core build too (the parent of Task 17's commit plus that commit, built in a checkout the owner makes); (b) query by bundle ID (MacOsOptions accountName set to the bundle identifier), which moves the installed app's own key to a new item and needs a one-time copy of the old one; (c) answer the question for the copy at each run (Deny gives a null key but adds the wait to every launch's home-usable; Always Allow adds the copy's ad hoc signature to the saved key's ACL, the write record f8e77ca8 named).","summary":"The re-identified copy dev.empathic.clax.perf still asks for the installed app's saved API key: the login keychain is not kept per container, so a measured launch waits on macOS's keychain question","tags":["review","time-to-usable","needs-device","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:43:04.833792Z","id":"9bbe2b8da5103d265260a25923fd4b813dfa7ee634c26679551e7aaa05da7dec","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f8e77ca85d183cc41ea0defc352026e3dd581ab3af4e9bccd9d9f335cd5dfc6d","summary":"Decided by the owner, 2026-10-20: measure a re-identified copy. The script's unpacked copy gets CFBundleIdentifier dev.empathic.clax.perf and is signed again ad hoc keeping its entitlements, so it runs in a container of its own; the script deletes that container at the end; it never touches dev.empathic.clax's container or the owner's saved key.","tags":["status:decided","time-to-usable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:43:04.834120Z","id":"711d10b72dbea3bd2013bdc4ddffa22e7b9204124a4e8c1e045c8f54b0738b9f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:86538601c","summary":"Done as the owner decided on 2026-10-20, in 86538601c: scripts/perf-app-launch.sh --macos copies the build under target/perf/clax-perf-<sha>, sets the copy's CFBundleIdentifier to dev.empathic.clax.perf, signs it again with codesign --force --sign - --preserve-metadata=entitlements,flags,runtime, runs it without CLAX_APP_DIR, removes ~/Library/Containers/dev.empathic.clax.perf before the first launch and at the end, and refuses a CLAX_PERF_CONTAINER of another name. bazelisk test //scripts:perf_app_launch_test passes (19 checks), among them '--macos: the copy, never the app given, is re-identified as dev.empathic.clax.perf and signed again keeping its entitlements; it runs without CLAX_APP_DIR', '--macos: the copy's container is removed before the first launch and at the end' and 'a container not named dev.empathic.clax.perf is refused before any launch'. One launch of a re-identified local build showed the sandbox making ~/Library/Containers/dev.empathic.clax.perf, and dev.empathic.clax's preferences plist kept its mtime. The keychain part does not hold: the copy still asks for the installed app's saved key item, record 30b78596.","supersedes":"f8e77ca85d183cc41ea0defc352026e3dd581ab3af4e9bccd9d9f335cd5dfc6d","tags":["reason:fixed","time-to-usable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:43:18.997517Z","id":"37bc08c43cc90856b598d426cdd3a80fae42b3632fcc65d6f7074efade4b3538","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:246e5865a","summary":"Fixed in 246e5865a: after the dropped launch's home-usable, scripts/perf-app-launch.sh waits (at most the cap) for <container>/Data/Library/Caches/dev.empathic.clax.perf/home/home-snapshot.bin on macOS and for run-as dev.empathic.clax ls cache/home/home-snapshot.bin on Android before stopping the app, and stops the run when none is kept. The test's fake app now writes home-cover only when a snapshot exists and takes it a second after home-usable; before the fix its loop printed app_home_cover_ms runs 0, missing 3, and after it bazelisk test //scripts:perf_app_launch_test passes with '--macos: four launches for three runs, the first dropped once its snapshot is kept, so each measured launch has its cover' (cover median 25, p90 30, runs 3, missing 0) and 'a dropped launch that keeps no snapshot within the cap stops the run before any measured launch'.","supersedes":"f729ccc3cbe0db5380c388921f1fced9153dd0382f7384e0fb064750e22ed66d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:43:19.518411Z","id":"774366c644d4d0232a713c34c0e6413687af59f299f120feeba37d1aad46207e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ddf688c03","summary":"Fixed in ddf688c03: --macos stops before the first launch while ioreg reports CGSSessionScreenIsLocked=Yes; on both platforms a dropped launch without home-usable within the cap stops the run; with CLAX_PERF_JSON each timing's missing count is its own perf-log line (unit launches); --record exits 1 and writes nothing when any launch is missing. bazelisk test //scripts:perf_app_launch_test passes with 'a locked screen (CGSSessionScreenIsLocked) stops the run before any launch', 'a dropped launch without home-usable stops the run after one launch, its app stopped', 'CLAX_PERF_JSON: each median and p90 for perf-log.sh, the p90s beside their budgets, and the launches missing' and '--record refuses a run with a launch missing and writes nothing'; each failed before the change.","supersedes":"8c98876b6e103519553d2fe0c008cfe0e74f81577858f1136db9bd08ad97ac5a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:43:20.026010Z","id":"3224eb17a4460eb11f87cb2f819f85214f5aac5997fd2dbbcea112a5e6d68bef","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a1daaa866","summary":"Fixed in a1daaa866: the JSON gains build {commit (--commit, else HEAD when the script built the app), app, sha256, version (CFBundleShortVersionString (CFBundleVersion), or versionName (versionCode) on Android)}, and scripts/perf-log.sh record stamps PERF_COMMIT when set. bazelisk test //scripts:perf_app_launch_test passes with '--macos: the JSON names the build measured: --commit, the app, its digest and its version', 'five launches: ... the build named by --commit' and 'perf-log.sh record names PERF_COMMIT's build'.","supersedes":"f595e91d68eb4e37f90fdb7eedf76158710dfb00fe1fd21d20ecade5f7d04584","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:43:20.542749Z","id":"f7cd2ffa53d0e8587197e900abb2eb33abb66f171f479bb8525b084705a74070","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:83144f237","summary":"Fixed in 83144f237: scripts/perf-app-launch.sh reads and records its budgets in web/perf/app-budget.json (created empty), so web/perf/usable.perf.ts's file holds web budgets only. bazelisk test //scripts:perf_app_launch_test passes with 'the app's budgets are kept in web/perf/app-budget.json, apart from the web's budget.json that usable.perf.ts reads', which failed before the change.","supersedes":"76129aca76494b5d10b4a802df78628eb12ad8704277fc8fa46ed4601641233c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:43:37.728230Z","id":"67928c9c54efaf39c4cae9c32fe6b17007eebbdfdd926dd5210e3975c27661c0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:436605d23","summary":"Fixed in 436605d23: docs/usage.md ('Measuring the home screen's start', 'Taking the launch baseline') and plan Task 16 Step 5 (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-19-in-process-core.md) now append with scripts/perf-log.sh record --append target/perf-log.jsonl under PERF_COMMIT=<the measured build's commit> (PERF_COMMIT honoured since a1daaa866), measure the daemon build's zip with --app and --commit from this checkout (built in a checkout the owner makes; an agent makes none), and take the phone's baseline on the installed build without just app-phone. Record 42a67fae's fix is rewritten to the same procedure.","supersedes":"7d49f12ad45500df26366798af0aedb3b9c33c060669df84dcce3ec707fa9cba","tags":["reason:fixed","time-to-usable","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:43:37.784410Z","id":"b7e720a7147b77e678f73331eaf5175b74ca5ab5b74e6ae73fd2860f1eb51ce5","body":{"detail":"//apps/clax_app:macos_app at 79cecdcc6, launched with a scratch CLAX_APP_DIR: a sample of the app showed its flutter_secure_storage queue in SecItemCopyMatching -> SecKeychainItemCopyContent for the whole run, ioreg reported CGSSessionScreenIsLocked = Yes, the daemon was never spawned and no timings.jsonl was written. The script now stops at once on a locked screen (ddf688c03) and measures a copy re-identified as dev.empathic.clax.perf (86538601c), which still asks for the same saved key item (record 30b78596, an open decision): the macOS baseline waits on that decision. The --android path has not run against a device or emulator either.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":64},"end":{"line":68},"content_hash":"4cf41a9b319ed9aaa140b7946796968e332f4a4e5154ae8deb13c76e5a65be8d"},"suggested_fix":"The owner's steps in docs/usage.md ('Taking the launch baseline'): name the daemon build's commit C (the branch head before Task 17 lands, else the parent of Task 17's commit); build its zip with just app-macos in a checkout of C the owner makes and keep it as target/perf/clax-macos-$C.zip; with the screen unlocked and record 30b78596 decided, CLAX_PERF_JSON=target/perf/app-launch-before.json scripts/perf-app-launch.sh --macos --app target/perf/clax-macos-$C.zip --commit $C --runs 9 --record --i-know-what-i-am-doing; then PERF_COMMIT=$C scripts/perf-log.sh record --append target/perf-log.jsonl target/perf/app-launch-before.json. On the phone, with its owner present, the build installed now (never just app-phone): --android --commit <its commit> --record, logged the same way. Commit web/perf/app-budget.json with both runs' medians and p90s.","summary":"No launch baseline is recorded and web/perf/app-budget.json has no app_home_usable_ms or app_home_cover_ms budget: every macOS launch of the ad hoc signed daemon build waited on the login keychain prompt for the saved API key while the screen was locked","supersedes":"42a67fae7d355b48ccdcd7e2fc49aef86d4b4601a6ee97489da7e7e1f617736d","tags":["time-to-usable","needs-device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:55:07.581680Z","id":"e6eb2054034a54e86b6e5a3209464df8c848dfdf474443b4b60f6c9ebf1af083","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"30b78596a6d5011566bd47ba07c4ce4c542886979089bb577affc6979907011b","summary":"Decided by the owner, Alex Kesling, on 2026-10-20: option (a). With CLAX_APP_NO_KEY=1 in its environment the app reads no saved API key (no keychain access at all, as if none were saved), so a launch measure never touches the owner's key and never prompts.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:55:07.581966Z","id":"3c5c4396f235a0e877632e91483ee425fbcb211448e66960a3d7465311d35254","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a6339ce54","summary":"Done as decided, in a6339ce54: FlutterSecureKey (apps/clax_app/lib/platform/secure_key.dart) takes withheld, set in platformServices (apps/clax_app/lib/main.dart) from FlutterSecureKey.withheldBy(Platform.environment), read once at launch; withheld, read() answers null without touching flutter_secure_storage and write() throws a StateError. scripts/perf-app-launch.sh --macos runs each launch as env -u CLAX_APP_DIR CLAX_APP_NO_KEY=1 <copy>/Contents/MacOS/Clax; on Android the variable does not reach the app and a Keystore read asks nothing, as the script's header says. bazelisk test --nocache_test_results //apps/clax_app:platform_secure_key_test //apps/clax_app:daemon_supervisor_test //apps/clax_app:dart_analyze //scripts:perf_app_launch_test: 4 tests pass, among them 'a withheld key reads as none and refuses writes, never reaching the secure storage', 'with the key withheld (CLAX_APP_NO_KEY=1) the daemon starts with no key, and the secure storage is never asked' and '--macos: ... every launch runs without CLAX_APP_DIR and with CLAX_APP_NO_KEY=1' (19 checks). Not yet run against a real build: the first launch of a build that includes a6339ce54 shows whether the keychain question is gone.","supersedes":"30b78596a6d5011566bd47ba07c4ce4c542886979089bb577affc6979907011b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/perf-app-launch.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T11:55:07.639016Z","id":"5938f721fff1c037e2aa587a976335910d73f5d7058a49cfde4f3c4361d69480","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"b7e720a7147b77e678f73331eaf5175b74ca5ab5b74e6ae73fd2860f1eb51ce5","summary":"The macOS baseline no longer waits on record 30b78596: a6339ce54 makes the app read no saved key under CLAX_APP_NO_KEY=1, which scripts/perf-app-launch.sh --macos sets for every launch. docs/usage.md ('Taking the launch baseline') step 1 now names a build C that includes a6339ce54 (checked with git merge-base --is-ancestor) and comes from before 'Run the app on the embedded core'; a build from before a6339ce54 still asks for the keychain.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/app-macos-dev.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:34:12.510892Z","id":"59d6adc1138773f65dc71c671169d7590e52b6802685a8d727e9eb263a04100e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f4d07c9a4","summary":"Fixed in f4d07c9a4: scripts/app-macos-dev.sh runs scripts/patch-pub.sh --i-know-what-i-am-doing after packing the home bundle and runs flutter run with PUB_CACHE=apps/clax_app/build-native/pub-cache. Its dry run lists both; its build steps run for real on 2026-10-20 (patch-pub.sh --i-know-what-i-am-doing, then PUB_CACHE=<that cache> flutter build macos --debug in apps/clax_app) printed 'patch-pub: patched webview_flutter_wkwebview 3.27.0' and '✓ Built build/macos/Build/Products/Debug/Clax.app': the Mac runner compiles against the patched plugin.","supersedes":"67b692abc6583acd375a8de32b532ba314b3c0559b3787b50642692397dd94d4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/patch-pub.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:34:12.578923Z","id":"097efc2b85f7eae673a7b5aa450a682e75a3779253caee63ef3cbd1cdca87200","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f4d07c9a4","summary":"The acting run ran on 2026-10-20 (through the build steps of scripts/app-macos-dev.sh as of f4d07c9a4): flutter pub get --enforce-lockfile into apps/clax_app/build-native/pub-cache left pubspec.lock unchanged (git status), the patch applied ('patch-pub: patched webview_flutter_wkwebview 3.27.0'), and flutter build macos --debug with that PUB_CACHE built Clax.app with the runner's SchemeHost.swift, which uses the patched configurationHook.","supersedes":"3d901cf2ba8e71090d93ab5d0c9271d623e6611d0d71097365b936cf824d1b3e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/app-android-emulator.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:34:56.404581Z","id":"abd4d9f4831c4e6ffd5c30001fb27657e32f6195666527777a7bf1fa0821785e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9136f7833","summary":"Fixed in 9136f7833: scripts/app-android-emulator.sh's .running file records the serial, the PID, the PID's start time (ps -o lstart) and, once booted, its command (ps -o comm), and --start, --serial and --stop trust the PID only while both still match. bazelisk test //scripts:app_android_emulator_test --nocache_test_results PASSED; its cases 'a reused PID with another start time is neither reported nor stopped' and 'a reused PID with the start time but another command is neither reported nor stopped' fail on the script before 9136f7833.","supersedes":"5abbf5a5856d48ac87240afb0b5c876b5037b0a6838fb2d9c3b208805b878c9f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/app-android-emulator.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:34:56.872883Z","id":"70ffad40ef5cb1eebe64c5cffb4a2b8692d4867be669b6cbfc9e2dc641556e04","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:21b5408fe","summary":"Fixed in 21b5408fe: from the emulator's spawn until it has booted, an EXIT trap (with INT, TERM and HUP turned into exits) stops that emulator by its PID and its adb server on port+10000 and removes the .running file. bazelisk test //scripts:app_android_emulator_test --nocache_test_results PASSED; its cases 'an emulator that exits while booting leaves no adb server and no .running file' and 'an interrupted boot stops the emulator and its adb server' (a SIGTERM to --start during the boot wait) fail on the script before 21b5408fe. The Android spike run of 2026-10-20 ended with the emulator's PID gone and nothing listening on 15554.","supersedes":"31561f1121a4b35b580d3d41fdcc408ed33410559201aed58cd8f83e2e11e081","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/app-android-emulator.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:34:57.272922Z","id":"b48cbe2776fdda2660b105dd9addb896d4e44ff8a553ae4fff42145c1311718a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:887ba08d4","summary":"Fixed in 887ba08d4: --start boots with -read-only, --clean removes target/android-avd and target/android-home (refusing while the emulator runs), and docs/bazel.md says the system image is kept once per user in Bazel's repository contents cache (4.3 GB unpacked, its 1.9 GB zip in the content-addressable cache). After --clean and one run of bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_android_scheme_spike (PASSED in 43.3s), target/android-avd was 32 MB, against 1.4 GB after the run before. //scripts:app_android_emulator_test covers --clean.","supersedes":"c0e0d9f797ba3393cce36adf41e7a06641f838153db0074c7432416b4b1bafd1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/run.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T22:27:54.051708Z","id":"f6ee89f7c9e8e65c63a367b7dd436ae72480b6598505b23ba4a0fbd5c36ebc82","body":{"detail":"scripts/run.sh's native app-test (and scripts/quality_gates.sh's app lane) runs apps/clax_app/tool/check.sh with no CLAX_EMBED_LIB, and the real tests open the core only from it (apps/clax_app/test/support/paths.dart claxEmbedLib, test/core/core_real_test.dart: skip 'CLAX_EMBED_LIB is not set'). Under Bazel they run against //crates/clax-embed:clax_embed_host. A native run therefore reports them skipped, not run.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":283},"end":{"line":286},"content_hash":"a3afb51ff2fd5ea5c819e7bfa8a5ac7c8f3d93c97b068015208a74d2b084cc8f"},"suggested_fix":"Build the host core with cargo build -p clax-embed and pass CLAX_EMBED_LIB=$PWD/target/debug/libclax_embed.dylib (or .so) to tool/check.sh.","summary":"Natively, app-test's flutter test gives the *_real_test.dart files no CLAX_EMBED_LIB, so they skip","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/check-ios-spawns.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T22:27:54.170348Z","id":"f94ad7f1ca4c67f7b8053d31ef3c15f2b9a9fcc9dcd08d0c12e10bcda571e096","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3b20d204f41fa4f90a613de126e38f783a5c2ad964e33ea5af572f6b86c1806f","summary":"crates/clax-ios is deleted: the iOS arms now compile in //crates/clax-embed:ios_build_test, which builds clax-embed and its dependencies (clax-server, clax-mcp, clax-core, clax-realtime) for aarch64-apple-ios and aarch64-apple-ios-sim (bazelisk test //crates/clax-embed:ios_build_test: PASSED on e45ef2491's tree), and check-ios-spawns.sh scans clax-embed in clax-ios's place. Whether an allowed function runs nothing on iOS is still reviewed per entry.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-clax.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T22:27:54.170626Z","id":"1b456793b5361f09bfe10dbd25a205c9a81d5d342924df72bf8f3e25b971de04","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"688a1a4ebb8462d93bf00159a978838a27eef14d5b16f26e7a891a1ed0598577","summary":"Still so for the core: the script now builds clax-embed, whose web UI comes from crates/clax-embedded/src/web.rs (RustEmbed over $CLAX_WEB_DIST_DIR, and the workspace's rust-embed in Cargo.toml has no debug-embed feature), so 'scripts/build-app-clax.sh android --debug' places a jniLibs/<abi>/libclax_embed.so that reads web/dist from the build machine. just app-clax-native is gone; the script is run directly. Bazel's //crates/clax-embed:clax_embed_android_* are always optimized.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/build-app-clax.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T22:27:54.170878Z","id":"12de43040d222240062ed5b3c6f4158bca0bcda42258635d148f92e90776881a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"87888a6c851e5ee5685c4f01036464e501fb2d73299c977a5885e25f3de84ec2","summary":"The path is now scripts/build-app-clax.sh:61, and the script builds clax-embed; just app-clax-native is gone, so this applies when the script is run directly (or through the -native app recipes).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
